+### Removing a user from an organization
+
+`DELETE /orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}` removes the user from the memberships of
+every project of the organization (offboarding).
+
+- The organization must be the caller's own; another organization → 404.
+- Only org admins may do this; other callers of the organization → 403.
+- The user must be a user of that organization; otherwise → 404.
+- The memberships are deleted, including those in archived projects. This is
+  the one exception to "archived projects reject all writes": a departing
+  member has to be removable even from an archived project.
+- The user's tasks in those projects are unassigned, so the assignee rule
+  still holds.
+- The user row is kept. Removing a user that is already in no project → 204.
+
